In article <33691@skye.dcs.ed.ac.uk> pwg@dcs.ed.ac.uk (Paul Goldberg) writes:
|How about enhancing the combat capabilities of the player by
|adding a #grab command which allows you to attempt to sieze
|and pick up a monster in the direction you specify. Of course
|this would require a new "livestock" slot in your pack inventory.
|You could then put the beastie in a bag, or throw it, or eat it
|alive, or whatever.
|
|Paul.

Of course, this only works for size small monsters when your strength is
under 15, and medium size for under 19.  And, your carrying capacity has to
have the room to spare (if the corpse weighs $1500, and you can only carry 
another $1200, you can't grab it).  When polymorphed into a giant or similar
creature, you can grab up to your carrying capacity.  And, when holding a
live one, they can't miss you.  Of course, one has to figure in the extra
chance of being fatally stabbed by that goblin as you try to take 'im alive:)

